Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:34:06 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 28/58] Sync the liveness engine: pad-2026.10.5 (int8 SFace),
 lazy matcher, store base

Engine jars and models from Mosip26 3eea3dc (fix round 2):
- the binding threshold default is 0.45;
- preload() verifies all five files but builds only the four per-frame
  sessions; the face matcher (MATCHER) session is built on first use or
  by OnnxFaceAnalyzerFactory.warmUpMatcher();
- ModelStore.install(staged, bundled, keys) seeds the bundled bundle as
  the rollback base when the store is empty or older, and removes the
  older bundles;
- the bundle is pad-2026.10.5: OpenCV Zoo's int8 SFace,
  face_recognition_sface_2021dec_int8.onnx (9,896,933 bytes), replaces
  the fp32 file (38,696,353 bytes). The analyzer jar is 13.5 MB (42.4 MB).

LivenessServiceHolder uses the new engine API:
- preload(), on the background thread, then builds the matcher session
  (warmUpMatcher) and logs both times;
- installModelBundle() calls install(staged, assets, keys): the staged and
  the bundled bundles are verified first, the staged one must be newer
  than both, and an empty or older store gets the bundled models as its
  rollback base (the special case for an empty store goes).

On the phone (debug build): "bundle pad-2026.10.5 verified and loaded in
222 ms", then "face matcher session built in 34 ms" (fp32 four sessions:
427-526 ms; fix round 1, five sessions: 504 ms).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
